  "notes": "Biomechanics option, University Park (of four options -- Biochemical, Medical Imaging and Devices, Biomaterials are the others, each with its own distinct prescribed courses and elective-slot names/counts; would need separate degree-plan JSON files to model). Fetched the 2022-2023 archived bulletin directly (Suggested Academic Plan and Program Requirements tabs) and confirmed the Biomechanics option's own required courses and suggested-semester sequence are byte-identical to the 2026 edition: BME 201/301/303/313/401/402/403/408/409, EMCH 210/212/315/316, plus 9 Biomechanics-Option-elective credits and 3 Related-Elective credits, same semester placement, 131 total credits. Real difference found (informational, does not affect this file's sequence): the archived 2022-2023 bulletin's 4-option lineup was named 'Biochemical, Medical Imaging and Devices, Biomaterials, Biomechanics' -- the current (2025-26 onward) bulletin renamed/restructured the other three into 'Biopharmaceutical, Medical Imaging, Medical Device Design'; the Biomechanics option modeled here kept its name and required-course list unchanged across the rename. Could not re-verify the 'Biomechanics Elective' regex match list (BME 410/413/419/443/444/446/494H/496, EMCH 400/402/403/409/416/446/461, ME 360/370/461, EDSGN 452/453) against a historical department elective-list page for 2022 -- that page is the live BME department site, not part of the bulletin archive, so it has no per-year snapshot; carried forward unchanged from BME-2026.json since the bulletin's own 'Biomechanics Option electives' wording is unchanged. 'Related Technical Elective' and 'Science or Engineering Elective' wiring also carried forward unchanged: the archived bulletin states both requirements in the same words as 2026. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair (unrelated to this year's own research, carried forward as-is from 2026): CHEM 110's real catalog prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan, so MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester